{
  "esm": "2.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "lanes_time_observed_whole_domain",
    "description": "Observeds of t on the lane set x that read other cells of x: q[i] = sum over m of s[m] / (i + m), and p, a makearray whose second region reads s one cell back (p[1] = cos(t), p[i] = s[i - 1]), with s[i] = cos(t + i). Neither has a lane form, so a lane program computes them, and the observed s they read, over the whole domain once per call, at one time: a call at one time equals the whole-domain program, and a call whose lanes are at different times is refused naming them. The state equation also reads r[i] = sin(t i), an observed of t with a lane form.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciAST test suite"
    ],
    "created": "2026-11-27T00:00:00Z",
